# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and tested on Linux, so line endings are
# pinned here rather than left to each contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
# Without this, a Windows checkout commits CRLF into lilith.sh and Linux then
# fails with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" -- which looks like a missing
# shell rather than a whitespace problem.

# Normalise every text file to LF inside the repository and on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch is the exception: cmd.exe parses labels and multi-line blocks
# by line, and an LF-only .bat can silently mis-execute.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Belt and braces -- these must stay LF even if the rules above are relaxed.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binaries: never EOL-converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.gguf binary
*.safetensors binary
